import html,json
E=html.escape
GROUPS=[('body','Mind & body','Expectation, feeling, healing and skilled action.'),('beyond','Minds beyond humans','Animals, living worlds and artificial systems.'),('practice','Cultivating mind','Memory, attention, sound and shared practice.'),('expression','Expressing mind','Poetry, diagrams, language and inner experience.')]
NOTES=[
('uisang','expression','Work','Uisang · Diagram of the Dharma Realm','The ocean-seal diagram: Buddhist thought expressed through a patterned poem. Read, trace, recite and interpret.','Poetry · art · Buddhism · Korean history','history.html','Edition and translated passage to select; the diagram is a work to study, not an illustration of modern neuroscience.'),
('jikji','expression','Work','Jikji · Pointing Directly to Mind','A Korean Buddhist work on mind and awakening. Its 1377 edition is the oldest surviving book printed with movable metal type.','Buddhism · print · art · technology','bank.html#jikji-text','Study the teachings as well as the printed object.'),
('placebo','body','Connection','Placebo / nocebo','Expectation, meaning and bodily experience. Compare placebo and nocebo responses without treating them as universal cures.','Psychology · medicine · anthropology','','A specific study or readable work remains to be selected. Symptom change and reversal of disease are different claims.'),
('healing','body','Claim to examine','“The only cure that works”','Compare claims about healing: what changes, what counts as evidence, and how meaning enters the experience.','Religion · psychology · history','','A contributed claim for analysis, not a medical assertion or treatment recommendation.'),
('ding','body','Work','Zhuangzi · Cook Ding','Practiced movement and cultivated attention. Bring the butcher’s account into conversation with music and sport.','Chinese thought · athletics · performance','bank.html#zhuangzi','A narrative of cultivated skill, not a physiological experiment.'),
('voice','body','Work','Mind-Body Awareness for Singers','Karen Leigh-Post’s work connects vocal performance with attention and bodily awareness.','Music · neuroscience · skilled action','https://www.lawrence.edu/people/karen-leigh-post/','Possible reading and demonstration; author participation is not confirmed.'),
('animism','beyond','Connection','Animism','Relationships and personhood involving animals, places and other beings. Begin with a named community and a specific work.','Anthropology · religion · environment','','Traditions differ; avoid treating animism as one universal belief.'),
('panpsychism','beyond','Connection','Panpsychism','Consider philosophical accounts that make mentality or experience fundamental and widespread in nature.','Philosophy · science · religion','','Distinct from animism; not a claim that everything thinks like a human. Reading to select.'),
('ai','beyond','Your question','What makes a mind “real”?','Minds and AI: distinguish intelligent performance, subjective experience, agency and moral standing.','Computing · philosophy · psychology','bank.html','These are different criteria. Fluent self-report does not settle them all.'),
('turing','beyond','Work','Turing · Computing Machinery and Intelligence','A concrete text for examining how we recognize thinking in a machine.','Computing · language · philosophy','possibilities.html#machine','Read the proposed test and its limits.'),
('animals','beyond','Connection','Animal minds & sensory worlds','Experience beyond the human: bats, sound, attention and the limits of our own perspective.','Biology · philosophy · environment','','A work and sensory-ecology encounter to select with relevant colleagues.'),
('levin','beyond','Research','Michael Levin · Coordination beyond brains','Living organization and cellular communication expand the conversation about cognition.','Biology · computing · philosophy','bank.html?researcher=Michael+Levin','Keep adaptive coordination distinct from evidence of felt experience.'),
('chant','practice','Work to select','Gregorian chant','A specific chant brings breath, memory, sacred language, architecture and collective listening together.','Music · Christianity · history','','Choose a named chant and recording with music faculty. Preserve its liturgical context; chant need not produce trance.'),
('trance','practice','Practice to study','Collective trance','Music, movement and transformed experience in a specific cultural setting. Study a documented practice with its context.','Anthropology · religion · performance','possibilities.html#trance','Contextual listening and analysis are already proposed; participation requires an appropriate facilitator and setting.'),
('memory','practice','Activity','Learn a poem by heart','Memorization as an encounter with language: sound, rhythm, recall and interpretation.','Poetry · music · learning','possibilities.html#poem-memory','Pair performance with close reading; offer accessible ways to participate.'),
('oliveros','practice','Work','Oliveros · Sonic Meditations','Text scores make attention and collective listening part of the musical work itself.','Music · attention · community','https://www.deeplistening.rpi.edu/deep-listening/','Select an authorized score and an appropriate facilitator.'),
('dhamma','practice','Work','Dhammapada · Verses on mind','Mental cultivation, attention and conduct within a Buddhist account of liberation.','Buddhism · poetry · ethics','bank.html#dhammapada','Keep the work’s religious purposes visible.'),
('dickinson-sky','expression','Work','Dickinson · The Brain—is wider than the Sky—','A short poem makes mind, world and scale available through the precision of poetic form.','Poetry · philosophy · neuroscience','bank.html#dickinson','Read the poem as a poem; its metaphors are not laboratory findings.'),
('dickinson-cleaving','expression','Work','Dickinson · I felt a Cleaving in my Mind—','Division, sequence and the effort to reconnect thought. A compact work for close attention to language.','Poetry · inner experience','','Edition to select; avoid retrospectively diagnosing the speaker or poet.'),
('dickinson-funeral','expression','Work','Dickinson · I felt a Funeral, in my Brain,','Sound, movement and the breakdown of sense make an inward experience take poetic form.','Poetry · music · psychology','bank.html#dickinson-funeral','Keep speaker, author and clinical diagnosis distinct.'),
('dream','expression','Work','Zhuangzi · The butterfly dream','Dreaming, transformation and the limits of a fixed account of self.','Chinese literature · philosophy','bank.html#zhuangzi-dream','A memorable entry into sustained reading of the Inner Chapters.'),
('borges','expression','Work','Borges · Funes, His Memory','A person who cannot forget makes perfect memory a problem for thinking.','Literature · memory · philosophy','https://thereader.mitpress.mit.edu/borges-memory-funes-the-memorious/','English titles vary by translation; fiction and empirical evidence remain distinct.'),
('dubois','expression','Work','Du Bois · The Souls of Black Folk','Double-consciousness, racial power and the social self. The Sorrow Songs make listening part of reading.','History · literature · music','bank.html#dubois','Preserve the work’s historical and political specificity.'),
('languages','expression','Encounter','Mind across languages & bodies','Heart, brain, spirit, intention and attention. Compare spoken words, signed languages and gestures.','Languages · art · anthropology','mind-words.html#meanings','Translations overlap without being identical; gestures need their own evidence.'),
('hyecho','expression','Work','Hyecho · A Buddhist pilgrimage account','Observation, interpretation and religious life across cultures. Korean Buddhist translation expertise belongs in this conversation.','History · translation · religion','bank.html#hyecho','The site credits Matty Wegehaupt’s contribution to the published translation.')]
def render():
 cards=[]
 for id,g,kind,title,body,areas,url,limit in NOTES:
  source=f'<a href="{E(url)}">Read more</a>' if url else '<span>Work or edition to select</span>'
  cards.append(f'''<article class="idea-note" id="note-{id}" data-group="{g}"><p class="note-kind">{E(kind)}</p><h2>{E(title)}</h2><p class="note-copy">{E(body)}</p><p class="note-areas">{E(areas)}</p><div class="note-actions" hidden><label><input type="checkbox" aria-label="Select {E(title)}"> Print this note</label><button type="button" class="copy-note">Copy note</button></div><details><summary>Context &amp; source</summary><p>{E(limit)}</p>{source}</details></article>''')
 filters=''.join(f'<button type="button" data-theme="{g}" aria-pressed="false">{E(t)}</button>' for g,t,d in GROUPS)
 return f'''<link rel="stylesheet" href="gallery.css"><script src="gallery.js" defer></script><section class="gallery-opening"><div><h1>MIND</h1><p class="gallery-deck">Works. Connections. Possibilities.</p><p>What is a mind? What makes a mind “real”?</p></div><div class="gallery-intro"><p>A collection for the Gallery Walk. Choose a few ideas, copy their wording onto Post-its, or print a set to cut apart. Add works and expertise as the conversation develops.</p><a href="proposal.html">Read the full proposal</a> · <a href="downloads/mind-qr.png">Get the QR code</a></div></section><div class="theme-guide">{''.join(f'<div><strong>{E(t)}</strong><p>{E(d)}</p></div>' for g,t,d in GROUPS)}</div><section class="note-tools" hidden aria-label="Note tools"><div class="theme-buttons"><button type="button" data-theme="all" aria-pressed="true">All ideas</button>{filters}</div><div class="print-tools"><button type="button" id="print-selected" disabled>Print selected notes</button><button type="button" id="select-visible">Select visible notes</button><button type="button" id="clear-selection">Clear selection</button><span id="note-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">0 selected</span></div></section><div id="note-grid">{''.join(cards)}</div><section class="own-note" hidden><h2>Add your own note</h2><p>Your added notes stay in this browser when storage is available. They are not published to the site. Printed notes are 3-inch squares; longer personal notes can extend below the square.</p><form id="add-note"><label for="own-title">Title or work</label><input id="own-title" required maxlength="90"><label for="own-text">Your note</label><textarea id="own-text" rows="3" required maxlength="240"></textarea><button type="submit">Add note</button></form></section><section class="gallery-bottom"><h2>Keep the conversation open.</h2><p>These are possible contributions, not a settled slate. Place names beside particular works after discussing their involvement, or label them as nominations. The public site does not list an endorsed faculty team.</p><p><a href="possibilities.html">28 detailed activity candidates</a> · <a href="history.html">Global history</a> · <a href="bank.html">Research bank</a> · <a href="syllabus.html">Model syllabus</a></p><a href="downloads/mind-gallery-handout.pdf">Earlier six-work handout (PDF)</a></section>'''
